# Project: FlyRank Frontend Capstone

## Stack
- HTML5, CSS3, JavaScript
- Framework: (سيتم تحديده لاحقًا - React/Vue/Vanilla JS)
- Styling: (Tailwind/Bootstrap/Custom CSS)

## Conventions
- Use semantic HTML5 elements
- Follow BEM naming convention for CSS classes
- Write clean, commented, readable code
- Prioritize accessibility (WCAG guidelines)
- Mobile-first responsive design

## AI Assistant Notes
This project is part of the FlyRank AI Internship — Front-End AI Engineering track.
Focus on production-grade UX, not generic templates.
## Contact Form / Validation Rules (learned from FE-03 workflow drill)
- Contact/settings forms must have exactly the fields specified in the task — do not add extra fields (e.g. Phone, Subject) unless explicitly requested.
- Email validation must use a proper regex (e.g. /^[^\s@]+@[^\s@]+\.[^\s@]{2,}$/), never a simple .includes("@") check.
- Every form must trim whitespace before validating required fields — whitespace-only input is not valid input.